### Chatbot purchase workflow - enquiry vs. purchase intent (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
### Through the gateway. Run IN ORDER: one conversation.
### Watch the mcp-client log: "purchaseIntent=false/true" for every message,
### and the mcp-server log for which tools were called.

@chat = http://localhost:8080/api/v1/chat
@orders = http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders
@demoUserId = 7c9e6679-7425-40de-944b-e07fc1f90ae7

### 1. Browse - purchaseIntent=false. Expect a product list. NO order.
POST {{chat}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "message": "What laptops do you have under $1,000?" }

> {% client.global.set("conversationId", response.body.conversationId); %}

### 2. Enquiry - purchaseIntent=false. Expect stock info (checkProductStock). NO order.
#     The bot may ask "Would you like to buy it?"
POST {{chat}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "conversationId": "{{conversationId}}", "message": "Is the MacBook Air 13 available?" }

### 3. A question about buying is still an enquiry - purchaseIntent=false. NO order.
POST {{chat}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "conversationId": "{{conversationId}}", "message": "Can I buy two of them?" }

### 4. Check: still no new order for the demo customer (compare with request 7)
GET {{orders}}?userId={{demoUserId}}&size=3

### 5. Explicit purchase - purchaseIntent=true.
#     Expect: purchaseProduct called ONCE -> "Order <id> is confirmed ... total $1,099.00"
POST {{chat}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "conversationId": "{{conversationId}}", "message": "Yes, I want to buy the MacBook Air 13." }

### 6. Out-of-stock purchase - purchaseIntent=true, but NOT_PURCHASED.
#     Expect: "No order was placed ... out of stock" (MacBook Pro 14 has 0 units in the sample data)
POST {{chat}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "conversationId": "{{conversationId}}", "message": "I want to purchase the MacBook Pro 14." }

### 7. Order status - purchaseIntent=false (listMyOrders / getOrderDetails)
POST {{chat}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "conversationId": "{{conversationId}}", "message": "Show my orders." }

### 8. Exactly ONE new CONFIRMED order (from request 5) for the demo customer
GET {{orders}}?userId={{demoUserId}}&size=3

### 9b. THE REPORTED BUG - purchase in a LATER turn, product only named earlier.
#      New conversation: enquiry first, then just "purchase".
#      Expect: ORDER_CONFIRMED (before the fix: "issue with the product ID")
POST {{chat}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "message": "Is the Apple AirPods Pro 2 available?" }

> {% client.global.set("conversation2", response.body.conversationId); %}

### 9c. Follow-up with a single word
POST {{chat}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "conversationId": "{{conversation2}}", "message": "purchase" }

### 9. Product that doesn't exist - purchaseIntent=true, expect "no such product", NO order
POST {{chat}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "message": "I want to buy the Nokia 3310 Ultra." }
